00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Evacuation: Using a vacuum pump to remove moisture and non-condensable gases
from the refrigerant circuit.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Triple Evacuation: Pull vacuum, break with nitrogen, repeat three times. More
effective at removing moisture.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Micron Gauge: Measures deep vacuum levels. System must hold below 500 microns.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Proper evacuation prevents acid formation
that destroys compressors. Cutting corners here causes callbacks.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: 500 microns or below is the target. And — Monitor for 10
minutes after closing the valve

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
What recovery level do you need on a system under 200 pounds using post-1993
equipment? Know that cold.

